WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.968
Jonnelle, thank you so
much for making time

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.937
to chat with us about the Fed.

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:09.376
This year in 2022,

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:12.712
the Fed has rapidly
increased its benchmark rate

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.118
which is a 15-year-high.

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:21.621
Talk about the different ways
ordinary people like me

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:25.291
are impacted by the Fed's
interest rate hikes.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:26.926
As they raise interest rates,

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:29.662
the goal is really to
make it more expensive

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:30.430
to borrow money.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:33.266
So of course we're feeling it
in the housing market already.

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:34.434
Mortgage rates went up

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:37.237
even before they actually did
the first rate increase.

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:40.073
But it does trickle down
to other kinds of loans.

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:42.042
The goal is to lower demand.

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:46.079
And that cooler demand should
in the end lead to lower prices.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.847
The Fed spends so much time

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.983
looking at economic forecasts

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:52.419
to suss out whether or not they
are making the right calls.

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:54.220
Do those indicators

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:58.158 position:63%
actually give them a good picture of how
our economy is doing? economy is doing?

00:00:58.158 --> 00:01:01.795
We know that the Fed rely
a lot on its forecasts.

00:01:01.795 --> 00:01:05.865 position:58%
Because of the pandemic and the
unusual circumstances that we are in,

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:07.534 position:56%
a lot of those forecasts were wrong.

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.569 position:58%
So what we hearing from officials now

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:11.538
is that they are going to be
looking more closely at

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:13.139
what is the economy doing.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:17.410 position:63%
Spending, home prices, inflation, hiring

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.946
and even some of these more
high frequency indicators,

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:22.215
how many people
are making reservations.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:24.417
One of the things the
Fed is working towards

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.820 position:64%
is achieving this idea of a soft landing.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.121
Can you talk about what that is

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:30.623
and how it's different
from a hard landing.

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:34.727
The goal for the Fed is
to bring inflation down

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:39.632
while minimizing the pain that we
would feel in our everyday lives.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:43.803
So they define that as like trying
to accomplish cooling inflation

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:46.172
without leading to a
spike in unemployment.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:49.509
Or at least limiting it
to a moderate increase.

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:51.377
As we head into 2023,

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:54.714 position:56%
what do we know about what the
Fed's terminal rate could look like?

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.349 position:59%
Just how high are these interest rates

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:57.484
supposed to get?

00:01:57.484 --> 00:01:59.052
Fed officials are saying that

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:00.653 position:56%
it's really uncertain at the moment.

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:03.490
And that it will depend on
what happens with inflation.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:05.625
If inflation starts to
come down more quickly,

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.627 position:56%
then rates don't have to go as high.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.863
If it takes a while,
they have to go higher.

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:12.198
Right now, the markets think
the rates will peak at

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:14.501
Some people think it could be

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:15.768
a little bit higher than that.

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:16.603
But we'll see.

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:17.604
Only time will tell

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:19.539
and it will depend on inflation

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:23.643 position:64%
and how much shift we see in the economy.

